There are $70$ haircuts in the whole, and we're thinking about $7$ of them.

$\begin{align}
\dfrac{7}{70}
&=\dfrac{1}{10} \cdot \dfrac{7}{7}\\\\
&=\dfrac{1}{10}
\end{align}$

There are $70$ haircuts in the whole, and we're thinking about $63$ of them.

$\begin{align}
\dfrac{63}{70}
&=\dfrac{9}{10} \cdot \dfrac{7}{7}\\\\
&=\dfrac{9}{10}
\end{align}$
